# A pattern here is read twice: by git, and by hatchling, which builds the wheel from
# whatever git would not ignore. So an unanchored pattern that happens to match a path
# inside the package removes that file from the wheel *and* from what the packaging test
# expects the wheel to hold — the two agree, and ship an incomplete package quietly.
#
# The rule that keeps them honest: leave a pattern unanchored only when the name is junk
# at every depth, so that dropping it everywhere is the right answer — hatchling's own
# EXCLUDED_DIRECTORIES and EXCLUDED_FILES, plus bytecode. Anchor everything else to the
# root it was always about. Nothing checks this — the suite cannot, because a violation
# makes both sides drop the same file and agree.

# Python. Bytecode and the in-tree virtualenv are junk wherever they appear. Hatchling
# drops `__pycache__` and `.venv` itself; bytecode it drops only by reading this line.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
/venv/

# Tool caches. Written in the rootdir, and dropped by hatchling at any depth.
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Coverage output. Root only — hatchling would ship a `htmlcov/` sitting in the package.
/.coverage
/htmlcov/

# Build artifacts. Root only, for the same reason.
/dist/
/*.egg-info/

# Throwaway design prototypes. Root only; local exploration artifacts are not package
# source.
/prototypes/

# macOS. Hatchling drops this from a build unconditionally, so the packaging test's
# two sides only agree on what counts as source if git drops it too.
.DS_Store

# local scratch directory
.scratch/
